"""
Project Name: Personal Finance Analyzer

Description:
This project is a Python-based personal finance application designed to
analyze bank-exported XLSX transaction statements and transform raw
transaction data into structured financial insights. The application
supports multiple bank statements, validates and combines transaction data,
classifies income, expenses, and transfers, categorizes transactions,
calculates financial and monthly summaries, evaluates financial health,
identifies subscription spending, and generates visual financial reports.

The application also uses AI to generate structured financial insights from
the calculated financial data. The project provides hands-on experience with
real-world financial data while developing skills in Python programming,
file handling, data validation, Pandas data analysis, Matplotlib data
visualization, financial-data modeling, AI integration, and software
engineering.

Objectives:
- Verify that one or more bank-exported XLSX statements can be selected,
  validated, opened, and combined successfully.
- Verify that required transaction columns are identified correctly.
- Verify that transaction dates are processed and the reporting period is
  determined accurately.
- Verify that transaction amounts are cleaned and converted into valid
  numeric values.
- Verify that transactions are classified correctly as income, expenses,
  transfers, or zero-amount transactions.
- Verify that transactions are assigned to the appropriate financial
  categories.
- Verify that total income, total expenses, net balance, and transaction
  count are calculated correctly.
- Verify that monthly income, expense, transfer, and transaction summaries
  are calculated accurately.
- Verify that financial health and savings rate are determined correctly.
- Verify that known subscription payments are identified and summarized
  correctly.
- Verify that financial summary tables and charts are generated and styled
  correctly.
- Verify that financial data is prepared and validated correctly before
  being provided to the AI model.
- Verify that AI-generated financial insights follow the required structure
  and use only the prepared financial data.
- Verify that generated financial reports can be saved successfully.
- Verify that invalid, missing, or inconsistent financial data is handled
  safely with appropriate exceptions and error messages.
"""
